# PSR-5c — named TenantRegistryAdminPort

## Why

PSR-5 item 5: control-plane admin access must go through a **named** interface
with capability/reason — not raw `getPrismaAdmin()` imports on the hot tenant
registry path.

Inventory classed these as `tenant_registry` (deferred from PSR-5b allowlist):

- `resolve-registered-tenant.ts` — cache-miss reads by id / subdomain / theme
- `update-tenant-registry-row.ts` — admin `tenants` update + cache invalidation

## Design (behavior-preserving)

New module: `apps/api/src/tenant/tenant-registry-admin.port.ts`

| Piece | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| Reason codes | `REGISTRY_RESOLVE_BY_ID`, `REGISTRY_RESOLVE_BY_SUBDOMAIN`, `REGISTRY_RESOLVE_THEME`, `REGISTRY_UPDATE` |
| API | `findTenantRowById`, `findTenantRowBySubdomain`, `findTenantThemeById`, `updateTenantRow` |
| Pool | still `getPrismaAdmin()` — **only** inside the port |
| Metrics | existing `recordAdminPoolRead`; plus `tenant_registry_admin_access_total{reason}` |
| Call sites | resolve + update import the port; **zero** direct `getPrismaAdmin` there |

No cache, mapping, or static-registry logic moves — only the Prisma admin I/O.

## Explicit non-goals

- Changing RLS / DATABASE_URL_ADMIN posture
- Rewiring finance `ALW-FIN-TENANT-ROW` onto this port (follow-up PSR-5d optional)
- Rewriting identity allowlist
- Audit event table writes (reason metric is the minimal audit signal this wave)

## Ratchet

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-5c-tenant-registry-port-smoke.mjs
node scripts/ops/psr-5-data-authority-inventory-smoke.mjs
node scripts/ops/psr-5b-admin-allowlist-smoke.mjs
```

After land:

- resolve/update must not match `getPrismaAdmin(`
- port file is the sole tenant-registry admin owner
- deferred_to_named_port entries in PSR-5b marked `closed_by: PSR-5c`
